---
Melion Bislcavret: 'Morning.
Alix LeThéque: ...
Melion Bislcavret: Could you move? I need to hit the button.
Alix LeThéque: I cannot.
-> Get out of the way.
    Melion Bislcavret: Move it, bub. I'm in a hurry.
    Alix LeThéque: ...
    Melion Bislcavret: I've got very important buissness to attend to, so–
-> Hit it for me.
    Melion Bislcavret: Hit it for me, then. 78th floor, exec suite.
    Alix LeThéque: ...
    Melion Bislcavret: Look, I've got places to be right now. So–
Alix LeThéque: I cannot let you past.
Melion Bislcavret: What.
Alix LeThéque: Do you know who I am, Sir?
<<if $knowsLeTheque==1>>
    Melion Bislcavret: Sure. LeThéque, right?
<<endif>>
Melion Bislcavret: You're from IT. You fix my computer sometimes.
Alix LeThéque: Sometimes?
Alix LeThéque: I graduated from KIT five years ago. I studied information systems and mechanical engineering.
Melion Bislcavret: Congratulations. I went to school too. Managerial accounting, by the way.
Alix LeThéque: I've worked here for three years and 41 weeks. 
Melion Bislcavret: So? I've been here sixteen.
Alix LeThéque: Biweekly, you encounter some kind of novel technological problem. Every 2.3 times per week, on average.
Melion Bislcavret: So I'm not a tech whiz. Sue me.
Alix LeThéque: Each time it takes me approximately 23 minutes to make the repair,
Alix LeThéque: and 18.5 minutes to explain the problem to you, in the hopes it won't happen again.
Alix LeThéque: Always in vain, of course.
Melion Bislcavret: Okay? I do my job and you do yours. That's life.
Alix LeThéque: I've spent 18,804 minutes at your desk, sir. That's 313 straight hours of my life.
Alix LeThéque: Excluding the time I spend singlehandedly preventing potential catastrophes from escaping the confines of your cubicle.
Melion Bislcavret: Wait, are you talking about...
-> The email scams?
    Melion Bislcavret: The emails I opened? How was I supposed to know they were fake?
    Alix LeThéque: Because I explained it to you, sir. On eleven separate occasions.
    Melion Bislcavret: They seemed convincing to me...
-> The password list?
    Melion Bislcavret: Keeping my passwords in a spreadsheet? How else am I supposed to remember them all?
    Alix LeThéque: You uploaded the file to your FierceBook profile. Three seperate times.
    Melion Bislcavret: So I clicked on the wrong picture. I was just trying out that 'networking' thing Renée mentioned...
-> The printer?
    Melion Bislcavret: (Actually, I probably shouldn't mention that one...)
    Melion Bislcavret: Wait, are you talking about...
    -> The email scams?
        Melion Bislcavret: The emails I opened? How was I supposed to know they were fake?
        Alix LeThéque: Because I explained it to you, sir. On eleven separate occasions.
        Melion Bislcavret: They seemed convincing to me...
    -> The password list?
        Melion Bislcavret: Keeping my passwords in a spreadsheet? How else am I supposed to remember them all?
        Alix LeThéque: You uploaded the file to your FierceBook profile. Three seperate times.
        Melion Bislcavret: So I clicked on the wrong picture. I was just trying out that 'networking' thing Renée mentioned...
Melion Bislcavret: Look, it doesn't matter. You fixed it!
Alix LeThéque: That's what I do with my degrees sir. My entire professional life is dedicated to dealing with you.
Alix LeThéque: I fix your information systems and engineer deterrences to your behavior.
Melion Bislcavret: Have you ever considered that you might be the problem?
Alix LeThéque: I have thoroughly considered every possibility. I briefly considered the idea that I'm already dead, and this is my eternal punishment for sins unrepented.
Alix LeThéque: But the P-value on that one is pretty low, all things considered.
Melion Bislcavret: Well, I've been promoted to the exec department. If you let me get there, you'll never see me again.
Alix LeThéque: You cannot fool me, Melion Bislcavret. It isn't that simple.
Alix LeThéque: You cannot be trusted with authority over the administrative system. You will infect the whole company with your incompetence.
Alix LeThéque: The scale of your ineptitude is almost supernatural. With more power, the support frames in this very building could begin to fail.
Melion Bislcavret: Don't be dramatic. Step aside.
Alix LeThéque: I am the last defense against catastrophic failure. Under no circumstances will you reach this control panel, sir. 
Alix LeThéque: Turn back, or be cut down.
Melion Bislcavret: (Ugh... again?)
Melion Bislcavret: Fine then. If that's how it's got to be.
Alix LeThéque: With the powers and duties vested in me by the office of integrated technology...
Alix LeThéque: I challenge you, Melion Bislcavret!
Alix LeThéque: En garde!
<<set $lethequeStart = 1>>
